  "_comment": [
    "Hand-curated side effects per command, read out of the handlers and the",
    "collaborators they call.",
    "",
    "Why this is not generated: effects are reached through objects held on self",
    "- self.pwm.off(), self.gcode.run_script(), self.journal.write() - and",
    "following those object graphs soundly is real static analysis. A detector",
    "that walks only the handler, or only self._methods, reports 'none detected'",
    "for NEBULAOS_BEEP (which drives the buzzer's PWM through a SysfsPwm object)",
    "and for SAVE_INPUT_SHAPER (which rewrites printer.cfg). That output is",
    "worse than no output: it reads as a safety assurance.",
    "",
    "So the generator no longer claims 'none detected'. A command with no entry",
    "here shows 'not determined', which is honest. Entries use these classes:",
    "  gcode      - runs G-code; can move the machine or change temperatures",
    "  hardware   - writes hardware directly (sysfs, PWM, I2C, EEPROM)",
    "  files      - writes or deletes files on the printer",
    "  config     - changes the saved Klipper configuration",
    "  persistent - changes state that survives a restart",
    "  readonly   - reports only; no effect found when the handler and its",
    "               collaborators were read"
  ]
}